            <ArticleTitle>Myofascial pain syndrome: an overview.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15360288.2014.997853</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Over the last few decades, advances have been made in the understanding of myofascial pain syndromes (MPSs). In spite of its high prevalence in the society, it is not a commonly established diagnosis. MPS is said to be the great imitator. This article puts some light on the various clinical presentations of the syndrome, on the various tools to reach to a diagnosis for commencing the treatment and on the treatment modalities that have been used so far.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
